From 0228f8269a91eb113ff1af2507ca5ff51fc4b402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:46:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Add colour/depth control (--control, --control-color,
 --control-depth, --control-end)

darask0/MOSS-Image-color-depth-control conditions generation on a flat-colour
region map and a depth map. Its video_embedder [3072, 384] replaces the DiT's
[3072, 128] and reads [noisy latent | colour-map latent | depth-map latent];
the rest is a rank-64 LoRA on the block linears and on the text embedder's
blocks, with bare keys. moss-mlx could not load either part: the LoRA key
pattern did not accept bare text_embedder.* keys and video_embedder.* raised.

- lora.py: apply_control() swaps in the wider video_embedder (never scaled)
  and applies the LoRA in group "control"; bare text_embedder.* keys resolve
  (TextBlock attributes); a control file given to --lora is refused with a
  pointer to --control.
- dit.py: embed() concatenates the control latents, zeros when absent (= no
  control). References get zeros too, i.e. the adapter's first 128 columns,
  the same embedder the target goes through.
- pipeline.py: Request.control_color / control_depth / control_end (default
  0.5). Maps are resized and centre-cropped like --init images and VAE-encoded
  (a grayscale depth map converts to RGB, as in training); a missing map is
  a zero latent. The maps go to every model call (both CFG branches, as
  trained) while i / n < control_end, zeros after. Combines with --init and
  --reference; turbo refuses control (its sampler has no control input).
- cli.py: --control ADAPTER, --control-color, --control-depth, --control-end;
  maps without --control and --control with --turbo are refused.

Checked: tests/test_control.py (adapter loads in its real key layout, shapes,
the maps change the output, zero-strength control with the original first
columns reproduces the plain model with and without references, end-fraction
zeroing for 0/0.3/0.5/1 incl. both CFG branches, validation); pytest 48 passed.
Real renders, compact + 8-step DMD, CFG 1, 1024^2, seed 1, a two-box layout
prompt from the repo's examples/two-people regions.json: with the colour and
depth maps both people stand exactly in the map's silhouettes (raised arm
included); 35 s denoise, 8.96 GB MLX peak (8.03 GB without control). At
control_end 0.5 the 8-step DMD run keeps the mannequin surface; 0.25 and
0.125 give real people in the same places.
Not checked: --init or --reference combined with control on real weights,
CFG > 1 runs, the Base transformer, colour-only or depth-only maps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
